                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "12039598",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197992251029",
                            "num_reviews": 5,
                            "playtime_forever": 212,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 212,
                            "last_played": 1408786522
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Disappointing, buggy. VERY BUGGY, puzzles are... Awful. There's no guidance in this game. You're basically running through rooms, you have to check every wall in every room to make sure you don't miss the place you're supposed to go.\nPuzzles basically mean \"Pick up these boxes and climb up this\", there's no variety at all.\n\nThe enemies are god awful. \"I WILL KILL YOU\" will be said about 80 times throughout this game, if not more. Your weapons are incredibly weak compared to their lores, considering your melee weapon is an axe that 'rips guts out'. It takes about 10 hits on the most common enemy to kill. 4 shots with a holy gun that's incredibly inaccurate.\n\nUpgrading mana is probably useless, it doesn't really help much at all. The game requires a lot of movement but you have stamina for sprinting so when you're stuck in a maze (Yes, a maze!) you can't sprint through it and instead have to hear the pathetic panting of your character.\n\nPhysics are bugged out as fuck. Infact in terms of bugs, I had to exit out of the game probably 4 times because I did a stage then have the game break itself. I got trapped in rooms, had a lift go without me with no sign of it coming back, have even died trying to break a forcefield with an explosive without even trying to use it!\n\nI recorded my gameplay of this - Around the end of the series the bugs happen more often. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_h04WcaROtI&list=UUctwhP4L0qZWJRF4r0vMQ7w",
